# SRG-APP-000439-AU-004310  -  CAT I
# The Central Log Server must be configured to protect the confidentiality
# and integrity of transmitted information.
#
# Generated from the benchmark and the assessment determinations. Edit this
# file to change how this requirement is assessed here; it is read at run
# time. Regenerating overwrites it.

id:              SRG-APP-000439-AU-004310
group:           V-206509
severity:        high
cat:             CAT I
determination:   APPLICABLE
grade:           C
decidable:       machine
confidence:      derived
cci:             CCI-002418
control_rev5:    SC-8

contribution:    Splunk can require TLS with an organization-issued certificate on the
                 Splunk-to-Splunk receiving port and on the forwarding output, pin the TLS
                 version and cipher list, and verify the receiving indexer's certificate.

governs:         inputs.conf - Configures inputs, distributed inputs such as forwarders, and file system
                 monitoring.
governs:         outputs.conf - Where this instance forwards its data, and how that connection is
                 protected.
governs:         server.conf - Core server settings, including the certificates and protocols used to
                 protect management and replication traffic.

check:           inputs.conf [splunktcp-ssl:<port>] serverCert non_empty
check:           inputs.conf [splunktcp-ssl:<port>] sslPassword non_empty
check:           inputs.conf [splunktcp-ssl:<port>] sslVersions equals tls1.2
check:           inputs.conf [splunktcp-ssl:<port>] cipherSuite matches ^(TLS_AES_(128|256)_GCM_SHA(256|384)|((ECDHE|DHE)-(ECDSA|RSA)-)?AES(128|256)-(GCM-|CCM-)?SHA(256|384))(:(TLS_AES_(128|256)_GCM_SHA(256|384)|((ECDHE|DHE)-(ECDSA|RSA)-)?AES(128|256)-(GCM-|CCM-)?SHA(256|384)))*$
check:           outputs.conf [tcpout:<target_group>] useSSL in true|1
check:           outputs.conf [tcpout:<group>] sslPassword non_empty
check:           outputs.conf [tcpout:<group>] sslVersions equals tls1.2
check:           outputs.conf [tcpout:<group>] sslVerifyServerCert in 1|true
check:           server.conf [sslConfig] enableSplunkdSSL in 1|true
# --- vendor verification: generated, do not edit by hand
corrected:       outputs.conf [tcpout:<group>] clientCert non_empty -> outputs.conf [tcpout:<target_group>] useSSL in true|1
vendor:          outputs.conf [tcpout:<group>] clientCert https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/manage-users-and-security/10.4/secure-splunk-platform-communications-with-transport-layer-security-certificates/configure-splunk-indexing-and-forwarding-to-use-tls-certificates
vendor:          outputs.conf [tcpout:<group>] sslPassword https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/manage-users-and-security/10.4/secure-splunk-platform-communications-with-transport-layer-security-certificates/configure-splunk-indexing-and-forwarding-to-use-tls-certificates
vendor:          outputs.conf [tcpout:<group>] sslVerifyServerCert https://help.splunk.com/en/data-management/splunk-enterprise-admin-manual/10.4/configuration-file-reference/10.4.0-configuration-file-reference/outputs.conf
vendor:          outputs.conf [tcpout:<group>] sslVersions https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/manage-users-and-security/10.4/secure-splunk-platform-communications-with-transport-layer-security-certificates/configure-tls-protocol-version-support-for-secure-connections-between-splunk-platform-instances
vendor:          server.conf [sslConfig] enableSplunkdSSL https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise/administer/manage-users-and-security/10.4/secure-splunk-platform-communications-with-transport-layer-security-certificates/configure-tls-certificates-for-inter-splunk-communication
# --- end vendor verification

external:        The certificate authority that issues the DoD approved certificates and
                 the key material placed on the host, which SPLK-CL-000450 verifies with
                 openssl outside the application
external:        Operating system permissions on the certificate and private key files
external:        Network layer protections such as IPsec or an SSL VPN, which the check
                 text accepts as alternatives to application TLS
external:        FIPS 140 validated cryptographic module supplied by the host operating
                 system, which decides the algorithms available to the pinned version and
                 cipher list

citation:        SRG-APP-000439-AU-004310 check text; SPLK-CL-000460 check and fix text;
                 SPLK-CL-000430 fix text; inputs.conf.spec:922-937, 986-1060;
                 outputs.conf.spec:647-712, 779-791; server.conf.spec:724-734
finding:         Splunk-to-Splunk traffic is not protected to the extent the product
                 allows: the receiving [splunktcp-ssl:<port>] stanza or the
                 [tcpout:<group>] output lacks a certificate, does not pin sslVersions to
                 tls1.2, permits a cipher outside the approved AES with SHA-2 list, or does
                 not verify the receiver's certificate.
